# Architecture

CipherForge follows a Modular Monolith architecture.

Modules are independent.

Each module owns:

- router
- service
- repository
- schemas
- models

Dependency flow:

Router

↓

Service

↓

Repository

↓

Database

Never violate this dependency order.

## Business Logic

Business logic belongs only in services.

Never place business logic inside:

- Routers
- SQLAlchemy models
- Database migrations

Repositories only perform persistence operations.

Routers only translate HTTP requests into service calls.

Shared functionality belongs in common modules.

Avoid circular dependencies.